# ── Files that must never enter a Docker image or git repo ────────────────

# Secrets — NEVER commit these
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local database. COPY . . would otherwise bake the development book —
# positions, cost basis, thesis text, profile, session hashes — into an image
# layer, where anyone with pull access can read it. A container must start with
# an empty DB and seed from config.
argus.db
argus.db-wal
argus.db-shm

# config.py's own local-override mechanism (see its `from config_local import
# ...` fallback). .gitignore already excludes this because it can hold real
# share counts, cost basis and private thesis text — the exact same leak
# argus.db above exists to prevent, and just as reachable: `docker build`
# is documented to run from the same directory a local `python main.py`
# session already populated config_local.py in.
config_local.py

# Agent tooling. .claude/worktrees/ holds a full second checkout of this repo.
.claude

# graphify's generated AST cache + wiki output — regenerable, adds nothing
# to a running container, and only bloats the image layer.
graphify-out/

# Python cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Git history (no reason to copy this into the image)
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Dev/editor artifacts
*.md
.vscode
.idea
*.log
